  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The centre $C$ of the circle $=(5,7)$ and the radius\n$=\\sqrt{5^2+7^2+51}=5 \\sqrt{5}$\n$\\mathrm{PC}=\\sqrt{12^2+5^2}=13 \\Rightarrow q=P A=13-5 \\sqrt{5}$\nand $p=P B=13+5 \\sqrt{3}$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/wf2Brex5t8NNHNPL_K5j5jggOlMntFYf9ncI-NbY-bM.original.fullsize.png\"/>\n$\\therefore$ G.M. of $p$ and $q$\n$=\\sqrt{p q}=\\sqrt{(13-5 \\sqrt{5})(13+5 \\sqrt{5})}$\n$=\\sqrt{169-125}=2 \\sqrt{11}$.",
    "image": null
  },
